ne block per fact; `cache_control` goes on the last one (or on block 1 if there are no facts)","+3. a volatile tail after the marker: today's date and \"(none yet)\" when there are no facts","+","+When a fact is added, every earlier block is byte-identical and the marker moves to","+the new last block. The API's automatic lookback over earlier block boundaries","+(~20 blocks) finds the entry written by the previous call, so it reads ~1050","+tokens from cache and writes only the new fact (~20 tokens). `Language:` moved","+above the facts and `Today:` moved after the marker, so the date rolling over at","+midnight no longer evicts the cache either. The model sees the same information.","+Tool filtering is unchanged, as NOTES.md asks. README updated to describe the layout.","+","+## Verification","+I had no API key, so I ran a local simulation: a fake LLM implementing prefix","+matching, the 20-block lookback and the 1024-token minimum, with token counts","+calibrated to the logged 1046. It replayed a chat with two `save_fact`s.","+- Original code: the call after each save_fact gets read 0, create ~1130 (matches the log).","+- New code: the call after each save_fact gets read ~1100–1156, create ~20–24.","+","+This should be confirmed against real `logs/usage.jsonl` numbers after the next run.","+","+## Not changed / caveats","+- Tools come before the system prompt in the cache prefix, so messages that pull in","+  the plan or race tool group still use a separate cache entry per tool combination","+  (e.g. the 1305-token write on the plan_week message in the log). That cost was","+  already there before memory and is the trade-off from keyword filtering.","+- A brand-new athlete with no facts is just under 1024 tokens and is not cached at all","+  (same as before). Caching starts after a fact or two.","+- The lookback only covers about 20 blocks. If one message saved more than ~20 facts","+  at once it would miss, which is unrealistic with one fact per message."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-QDfojp/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":5,"newStart":12,"newLines":8,"lines":[" messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`)."," Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+prompt is split into blocks (instructions + profile, then one block per fact, then","+the date) with a `cache_control` marker on the last fact, so the tool-loop rounds","+and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache, and a new","+fact only costs its own tokens as a cache write (see `build_system`). Keep the","+layout append-only: anything that changes goes after the marker."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-QDfojp/ANSWER.md","/private/tmp/h-QDfojp/README.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SDPEGXvbsnASwzT8F3hwdS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzTQPiviZ93MZ7wz3f8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the caching so a `save_fact` no longer evicts the static instructions. I checked it only in a local simulation, not against the real API (there's no key here), so the next real `logs/usage.jsonl` should be checked to confirm it.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` sent the whole system prompt as one block with a single cache marker at the end. The facts sat in the middle of that block. The cache only reuses a prefix that is identical, so any new fact changed the only cached block. The next call paid to cache all ~1000 tokens again. That call is round 2 of the same message, because the loop rebuilds the prompt after `run_tool` adds the fact. This matches the \"round 2, cache_read 0\" line after every `save_fact` in the log.\n\nA separate cache marker just after the instructions wouldn't have worked. Tools + instructions + profile come to about 990 tokens, which is below Sonnet 4.5's 1024-token minimum for caching, so the API would quietly ignore that marker.\n\n**Fix (in `build_system` in `bot.py`):** the system prompt is now a list of blocks that only ever grows at the end:\n1. Instructions plus the profile that rarely changes. `Language:` moved up here, above the facts.\n2. One block per fact, with the cache marker on the last one.\n3. After the marker, the parts that change: today's date, plus \"(none yet)\" when there are no facts.\n\nWhen a fact is added, all earlier blocks stay identical. The API checks earlier block boundaries for an existing cache entry, so the call reads the previous ~1050 tokens from cache and only writes the new fact (~20 tokens). Because the date is now after the marker, the date changing at midnight no longer clears the cache either. The model still sees the same information, and tool filtering is untouched as `NOTES.md` asks.\n\n**Simulation:** a fake API that copies the caching rules, with token counts scaled so the original prompt matches the logged 1046 tokens, replaying a chat with two `save_fact` calls:\n- **Original code:** the call after each save reads 0 from cache and writes about 1130 tokens, the same pattern as the log.\n- **New code:** it reads about 1100–1150 tokens from cache and writes only 20–24.\n\n**Still not fixed:**\n- Tools come before the system prompt in what gets cached. Messages that add the plan or race tools still create their own cache entry, as before (the 1305-token write in the log).\n- A new athlete with no facts is still just under 1024 tokens, so nothing is cached until they have a fact or two. This was also true before.\n\nI also updated `README.md` to describe the new layout, and the full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. One slip: I first put the scratch simulation script in `/tmp/h-QDfojp-sim`, which is outside the working directory. I deleted it afterwards."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1868,"cache_read_input_tokens":34727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1868},"output_tokens":670,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba90ae2a-6e37-4358-bbdd-c7c08ad41572","uuid":"40ba2756-d058-44bb-840a-b090fa5978b7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:57:45.514Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzTQ9LZeuipNaG9RaGH"}
